WEBVTT

WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:02.560
Hola.

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:06.880
Sorry.

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:08.640
I spoiled your lovely evening,

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:09.520
Cinderella….

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:10.680
That’s all right.

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:13.960
You know,

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:15.720
I wouldn't call a whole day

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:17.960
with Mason “lovely”.

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:19.320
I thought things were going

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:20.600
okay between you two.

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:26.920
It's impossible.

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:31.760
Grandpa.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:36.680
I think

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:40.000
Mason has done his part.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.080
The company is stronger

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:44.080
than ever and...

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:46.880
Please.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:50.600
Give me your blessing for a divorce.

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:54.280
He's not even a part of our family.

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:56.640
I'm begging you.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:01.800
No.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:03.560
I won't allow it.

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:10.560
I don't understand.

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:13.600
Why are you doing all this?

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:14.000
Yes.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:15.600
He’s probably good

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:18.320
at business, but

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:21.880
he's a stranger.

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:25.440
He is not the right choice for me.

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:29.240
It's not right for all of us.

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:30.520
I didn't choose him

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:32.080
for his business skills.

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:34.320
Then what for?

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:36.320
Don't you remember?

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:37.120
What?

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:42.000
Back when your parents were friends,

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:45.120
he often visited the mansion.

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:47.640
I kept an eye on him.

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:49.280
Mason was different

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:51.160
from other Powells.

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:53.840
Noble.

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:55.360
Strong.

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:58.320
He didn't care what others thought.

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:00.600
He always stood up for...

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:01.840
I'd say “good”.

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:04.880
But that sounds like a fairy tale.

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:08.440
Let's just call it justice.
